<title>BELGIUM: EU inflation fell to 1.5 percent in April.</title>
<headline>EU inflation fell to 1.5 percent in April.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average inflation rate for the European Union fell to 1.5 percent in April compared with 2.6 percent a year earlier, EUROSTAT reported on Friday.</p>
<p>The EU's statistics agency said Greece had the highest inflation in April at 5.7 percent, followed distantly by Italy with 1.9 percent. Rates were are follows:</p>
<p>EU - 1.5 percent</p>
<p>Belgium - 0.9</p>
<p>Finland - 0.9</p>
<p>France - 1.0</p>
<p>Luxembourg - 1.1</p>
<p>Germany - 1.2</p>
<p>Netherlands - 1.2</p>
<p>Sweden - 1.2</p>
<p>Austria - 1.3 (provisional)</p>
<p>Denmark - 1.5</p>
<p>Spain - 1.6</p>
<p>Portugal - 1.6</p>
<p>Britain - 1.6</p>
<p>Italy - 1.9</p>
<p>Greece - 5.7</p>
<p>Ireland's figure was unavailable, but was 1.7 percent in February, Eurostat said.</p>
</text>
